# A CANDIDATE: MEDCPT ON OUR LLAMA.CPP (the operator, 2026-11-26, through München: "Move
# both" - MedCPT's article encoder and its cross-encoder from OpenVINO to llama.cpp -
# "Validate all the models and port MedCPT").
# engine-pace.series line for line, then:
#   0034  a BERT text pair: with the model option pairs:true, VeGa's pair marker (an
#         embedding) and (query, document) (a rerank) become [CLS] a [SEP] b [SEP], cut
#         longest first to the load's context as Hugging Face's tokenizer cuts, the
#         second segment on token-type row 1 (the inner patch's pair_segments); a
#         [SEP] inside a first segment, or inside one text, is refused.
#         rerank_score:sigmoid answers the logit's sigmoid, as the OpenVINO backend did.
#         The converter keeps a BERT sequence classifier's pooler (MedCPT's
#         cross-encoder needs it), knows MedCPT's tokenizer, and writes the model's
#         GELU (bert.hidden_activation: "gelu" the erf GELU, which the graph then
#         computes): MedCPT's GGUFs are converted with this tree. A GGUF without the
#         key keeps the tanh GELU; without pairs:true no model's answer can move.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-pair.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE: a build and every gate again, and MedCPT's two models gated against
# their OpenVINO runs (docs/notes/medcpt-on-llama-cpp.md).
